WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:06.830
Hey David, what would a gun control compromise
look like between left and right?

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:09.080
Okay, let's do this.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:13.900
But we have to agree on a parameter first
because otherwise we're not going to get anywhere.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:19.700
Given that the second amendment exists, what
would a compromise look like if we are really

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:24.380
going to imagine a compromise that ignores
that the second amendment exists, even if

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.550
you don't like the Second Amendment, even
if you wish.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.340
The second amendment didn't exist.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:33.120
We won't get anywhere in imagining a compromise
that assumes the second amendment doesn't

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.840
exist, so we actually have to account for
that.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.660
When we think about what a gun safety compromise
might look like between left and right, but

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.670
I actually think there's a bigger problem
that we have to talk about.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.239
We could rattle off policies.

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:51.420
I could say, well the rite could concede universal
background checks and maybe we would ban some

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.149
high capacity magazines and the left would
have to concede something else.

00:00:55.149 --> 00:00:59.710
Then we would just argue about whether that's
too far left or too far right or too extreme.

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:00.710
We would get nowhere.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:04.510
In reality though, because there's a bigger
issue when you talk about a gun safety compromise.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:07.360
The problem here is not a practical problem.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:13.830
We could get together and workshop ideas and
come to some kind of hypothetical compromise

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:18.320
where both sides would give some stuff up
and get something and everybody would be sort

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.300
of unhappy, which is often the way a good
compromise ends up.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.810
The problem is we can't actually have that
conversation in good faith because number

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:31.740
one, everyone will see the compromise as a
Trojan horse and then immediately imagine

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:36.250
that the other side is going to just try to
get more and use the compromise as a way to

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.049
move the needle slightly.

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:44.760
And number two, you have a very well funded
market altering players like the NRA that

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:50.370
are a direct impediment to actually having
good faith conversations about this stuff.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:54.130
So it's actually a completely intractable
conversation.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.810
The causes of gun violence need to be addressed.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:59.650
The availability of guns needs to be addressed.

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.170
Mental health sure needs to be addressed.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:07.810
Gun Culture, the religion of guns is a massive
problem in the United States and for good

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:12.050
reason, no one trusts the other side to negotiate
in good faith.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:13.820
I'm not doing both sides.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.300
Ism, okay.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:20.650
The pro gun, more guns and more places side
is disgusting and they are extremely well

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:24.870
funded by these uh, gun manufacturers through
groups like the NRA.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:29.070
But whatever lists you and I can come up with
right now about what a compromise would look

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:31.800
like is effectively dead on arrival.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:36.879
Because groups like the NRA are very good
at getting even Donald Trump to say, oh I

00:02:36.879 --> 00:02:37.879
was for background checks.

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:39.819
Yeah, we're not doing that anymore.

00:02:39.819 --> 00:02:44.239
And number two, if you can seed anything,
the other side will say that's not in good

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:45.239
faith.

00:02:45.239 --> 00:02:49.920
You're just doing this in order to in six
months push for more and we're not going to

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:50.920
allow it.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:57.170
And this is unfortunately one of the areas
in which I am most pessimistic gun safety.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.200
I've talked already about climate change.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.470
If you've been watching the show, you know
that I am not particularly optimistic on the

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.570
climate.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:09.130
Gun Safety is another area where I am not
at all optimistic that we are going to make

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:16.420
it happen in a huge reason for that is the
just corrosive and disgusting effect of organizations

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.840
like the NRA.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.040
Uh, and I, I want to be convinced that this
could happen.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.500
I really do.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.519
But look at what happened with background
checks after Sandy Hook.

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:28.340
Look at all of the other examples.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:32.870
Uh, so I am not particularly optimistic and
I think whatever list we could come up with

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:39.280
would be taking an immediate back seat to
the partisan and lobbied in monied lobbying

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.220
interests that exist within gun safety.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.650
Let me know if I'm wrong and I should have
some more optimism on this.

